# Normalise line endings to LF everywhere, including Windows checkouts.
#
# Prettier writes LF (its `endOfLine` default), and CI runs `format:check` on
# Linux. Without this, a Windows clone can end up with CRLF working copies that
# fail the check locally while passing on CI — a confusing split that costs more
# time than it sounds like it should.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
